[[:db/retract 17592186180799 :answer-field/choices 17592186180800] [:db/retract 17592186180799 :answer-field/choices 17592186180801] [:db/retract 17592186180799 :answer-field/choices 17592186180802] [:db/retract 17592186180799 :answer-field/choices 17592186180803] [:db/retract 17592186180799 :answer-field/choices 17592186180804] {:db/id 17592186184177 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f9519db7-867b-512b-ba13-465c2170cdc3" "question-0c69e568-3aa6-590d-a547-523c7522fc27" "question-b816908c-853d-5e9e-8dd6-8428f48a97f8" "question-e1dd610f-bcb9-5742-82dd-3d71c2887869" "question-be4431be-3fe9-5dd2-82ee-71868596c05f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184078 :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent line to the polar curve $r = 1+2\\cos\\theta$ at $\\theta = \\dfrac{\\pi}{2},$ given that \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x} = -\\dfrac{\\cos\\theta  + 2\\cos(2\\theta)}{\\sin\\theta + 2\\sin(2\\theta)}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the equation of the tangent line to a polar curve at a point $P,$ we follow four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Calculate the derivative $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}.$\n\nIn this case, we're given that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x} = -\\dfrac{\\cos\\theta  + 2\\cos(2\\theta)}{\\sin\\theta + 2\\sin(2\\theta)}.\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find the slope of the tangent at $P.$\n\nThe slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{\\theta =\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )} \\\\  & =-\\frac{0+2(-1)}{1+2(0)} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Find the Cartesian coordinates of $P.$\n\nWe compute the $xy$-coordinates of $P$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =(1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =(1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =(1+2\\cdot 0)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0 \\\\ {y}_{1} & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =(1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =(1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =(1+2\\cdot 0)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of $P$ are $(0,1).$\n\n**Step 4**: Using point-slope form, find the equation of the tangent.\n\nWe find the equation of the tangent as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =2(x-0) \\\\ y & =2x+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/30/30b1aedfd6187ed1f936ef1faf25fcb8b99857103c656163a3e6897e5c6c5038.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184215 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c7a90aa7-52b9-549e-8c2d-341971525e44" "question-c83da1a3-053f-5553-bc32-57bdb774a02e" "question-4bd1b924-fea7-5666-9b66-85d3682d3092" "question-4b160342-1c9b-5cb6-9f7b-8bf55c5af2c6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184120 :question/problem "![](images/fc/fc3ec38b91c71be3e9638dfa0127f1baab5d11d30e6156d863b36758f6751e7d.png)\n\nFind the equation of the **normal** line to the polar curve $r = 1 - 2\\cos\\theta$ at $\\theta = \\dfrac{3\\pi}{2},$ given that\n\n$$\ny'(\\theta)  = \\cos\\theta-2\\cos(2\\theta) , \\qquad\nx'(\\theta) = 2\\sin(2\\theta) - \\sin\\theta.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the equation of the normal line to a polar curve at a point $P,$ we follow four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Calculate the derivative $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}.$\n\nIn this case, we're given that\n\n$$\ny'(\\theta)  = \\cos\\theta-2\\cos(2\\theta) , \\qquad\nx'(\\theta) = 2\\sin(2\\theta) - \\sin\\theta.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{y}^{′}(\\theta )}{{x}^{′}(\\theta )} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find the slope of the tangent at $P.$\n\nThe slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{\\theta =3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{3\\pi }{2}))}{(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{3\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}))} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\pi ))}{(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}))} \\\\  & =\\frac{0-2(-1)}{0-(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+2}{0+1} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Find the Cartesian coordinates of $P.$\n\nWe compute the $xy$-coordinates of $P$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =(1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =(1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}))\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =(1-2\\cdot 0)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0 \\\\ {y}_{1} & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =(1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =(1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}))\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =(1-2\\cdot 0)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of $P$ are $\\left( 0, -1 \\right).$\n\n**Step 4**: Using point-slope form, find the equation of the normal.\n\nWe find the equation of the normal as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =-\\frac{1}{m}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-1) & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (x-0) \\\\ y+1 & =-\\frac{1}{2}x \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{2}x-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-f9519db7-867b-512b-ba13-465c2170cdc3" :question/id #uuid "f9519db7-867b-512b-ba13-465c2170cdc3" :question/math-academy-id "q-149691" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent line to the polar curve $r=2\\theta $ at $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the equation of the tangent line to a polar curve at a point $P,$ we follow four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Calculate the derivative $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}:$\n\nIn this case, we're given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }.\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find the slope of the tangent at $P:$\n\nThe slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{\\theta =\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(1+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot 0)}{(0-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot 1)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Find the Cartesian coordinates of $P:$\n\nWe compute the $xy$-coordinates of $P$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =0 \\\\ {y}_{1} & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of $P$ are $(0,\\pi ).$\n\n**Step 4**: Using point-slope form, find the equation of the tangent:\n\nWe find the equation of the tangent as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-\\pi  & =-\\frac{2}{\\pi }\\cdot (x-0) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{2}{\\pi }x+\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/13/13bb063a7ae79887a653e5f1c330851e56183049f77853a6a1d35d4a023d615c.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-32043721-15c9-514d-b7b6-d5e1483be8e9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-32043721-15c9-514d-b7b6-d5e1483be8e9" :answer-field/id #uuid "32043721-15c9-514d-b7b6-d5e1483be8e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c0b85359-a2fd-5290-9f27-e1801e402b65" :answer-field/choices ["answer-208db34a-8dda-5860-8e33-45cf14a90efb" "answer-c0b85359-a2fd-5290-9f27-e1801e402b65" "answer-75e29095-66f1-5c3c-8ab7-a028112915df" "answer-5b70f284-3fe3-5a8d-bec9-048902b86dcd" "answer-45830fa0-a721-5aa1-8d77-6030c9c39893"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-208db34a-8dda-5860-8e33-45cf14a90efb" :answer/id #uuid "208db34a-8dda-5860-8e33-45cf14a90efb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{\\pi }x-\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c0b85359-a2fd-5290-9f27-e1801e402b65" :answer/id #uuid "c0b85359-a2fd-5290-9f27-e1801e402b65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{2}{\\pi }x+\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-75e29095-66f1-5c3c-8ab7-a028112915df" :answer/id #uuid "75e29095-66f1-5c3c-8ab7-a028112915df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{2}{\\pi }x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b70f284-3fe3-5a8d-bec9-048902b86dcd" :answer/id #uuid "5b70f284-3fe3-5a8d-bec9-048902b86dcd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{\\pi }x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45830fa0-a721-5aa1-8d77-6030c9c39893" :answer/id #uuid "45830fa0-a721-5aa1-8d77-6030c9c39893" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{\\pi }x-\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0c69e568-3aa6-590d-a547-523c7522fc27" :question/id #uuid "0c69e568-3aa6-590d-a547-523c7522fc27" :question/math-academy-id "q-141252" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent line to the polar curve $r=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta )$ at $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta )}{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta )}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the equation of the tangent line to a polar curve at a point $P,$ we follow four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Calculate the derivative $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}:$\n\nIn this case, we're given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta )}{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta )}.\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find the slope of the tangent at $P:$\n\nThe slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{\\theta =\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta )}{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta )} \\\\  & =\\frac{[3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})]}{[3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})]} \\\\  & =\\frac{[3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})]}{[3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})]} \\\\  & =\\frac{(3\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot 1)}{(3\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot 0-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})}{(-\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Find the Cartesian coordinates of $P:$\n\nWe compute the $xy$-coordinates of $P$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ {y}_{1} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of $P$ are $(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{1}{2}).$ \n\n**Step 4**: Using point-slope form, find the equation of the tangent:\n\nWe find the equation of the tangent as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-\\frac{1}{2} & =-\\sqrt{3}\\cdot (x-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\ y-\\frac{1}{2} & =-\\sqrt{3}\\,x+\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ y & =-\\sqrt{3}x+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/10/1018201037350f6bd231a384219d03c03fc1e2165a088e158c9ba2b2bfbb1022.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e0ec3545-9073-58ce-bcc7-3fa4b6d955fb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e0ec3545-9073-58ce-bcc7-3fa4b6d955fb" :answer-field/id #uuid "e0ec3545-9073-58ce-bcc7-3fa4b6d955fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0caec6d9-3660-5e5d-93f8-273e3177e9d2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0caec6d9-3660-5e5d-93f8-273e3177e9d2" "answer-99a09e67-57a3-595e-8038-9fd0c9ae9d5b" "answer-ff5bae98-5138-5fd6-bec2-d20b4cb20409" "answer-37dbe3a0-18a2-5453-a5d4-551f3906a5c0" "answer-c4bf4cb6-3664-5e42-9eac-88072f5bc8f7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0caec6d9-3660-5e5d-93f8-273e3177e9d2" :answer/id #uuid "0caec6d9-3660-5e5d-93f8-273e3177e9d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\sqrt{3}x+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-99a09e67-57a3-595e-8038-9fd0c9ae9d5b" :answer/id #uuid "99a09e67-57a3-595e-8038-9fd0c9ae9d5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\sqrt{3}x+\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff5bae98-5138-5fd6-bec2-d20b4cb20409" :answer/id #uuid "ff5bae98-5138-5fd6-bec2-d20b4cb20409" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{3}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-37dbe3a0-18a2-5453-a5d4-551f3906a5c0" :answer/id #uuid "37dbe3a0-18a2-5453-a5d4-551f3906a5c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{3}x+\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4bf4cb6-3664-5e42-9eac-88072f5bc8f7" :answer/id #uuid "c4bf4cb6-3664-5e42-9eac-88072f5bc8f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{3}x+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b816908c-853d-5e9e-8dd6-8428f48a97f8" :question/id #uuid "b816908c-853d-5e9e-8dd6-8428f48a97f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-351197" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation $y=f(x)$ of the tangent line to the polar curve $r={e}^{-\\theta }$ at $\\theta =0,$ given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }.\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of the tangent line is $y=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the equation of the tangent line to a polar curve at a point $P,$ we follow four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Calculate the derivative $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}:$\n\nIn this case, we're given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }.\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find the slope of the tangent at $P:$\n\nThe slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{\\theta =0} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡0-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡0+\\operatorname{sin}⁡0} \\\\  & =\\frac{0-1}{1+0} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Find the Cartesian coordinates of $P:$\n\nWe compute the $xy$-coordinates of $P$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={e}^{-\\theta }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={e}^{0}\\operatorname{cos}⁡0 \\\\  & =1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =1 \\\\ {y}_{1} & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={e}^{-\\theta }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={e}^{0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡0 \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of $P$ are $(1,0).$\n\n**Step 4**: Using point-slope form, find the equation of the tangent:\n\nWe find the equation of the tangent as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-0 & =-1(x-1) \\\\ y & =-x+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/66/6651277bec90a77e19d0bd6c1d1a464f636cf675cae25ad47a6f60a2a352002b.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f31d3a56-b5c5-51c7-b967-a906c3bde3cf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f31d3a56-b5c5-51c7-b967-a906c3bde3cf" :answer-field/id #uuid "f31d3a56-b5c5-51c7-b967-a906c3bde3cf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-03d8a6dc-a221-59ed-82be-92d1475ae262" :answer-field/choices ["answer-03d8a6dc-a221-59ed-82be-92d1475ae262"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03d8a6dc-a221-59ed-82be-92d1475ae262" :answer/id #uuid "03d8a6dc-a221-59ed-82be-92d1475ae262" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e1dd610f-bcb9-5742-82dd-3d71c2887869" :question/id #uuid "e1dd610f-bcb9-5742-82dd-3d71c2887869" :question/math-academy-id "q-362883" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation $y=f(x)$ of the tangent line to the polar curve $r=7\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ at $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡2\\theta .\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of the tangent line is $y=$\n{{field-1}}$x\\,-$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the equation of the tangent line to a polar curve at a point $P,$ we follow four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Calculate the derivative $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}:$\n\nIn this case, we're given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡2\\theta .\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find the slope of the tangent at $P:$\n\nThe slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{\\theta =\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Find the Cartesian coordinates of $P:$\n\nWe compute the $xy$-coordinates of $P$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =7\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =7\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =7\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\ {y}_{1} & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =7\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =7{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =7{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of $P$ are $(\\frac{7\\sqrt{3}}{4},\\frac{7}{4}).$\n\n**Step 4**: Using point-slope form, find the equation of the tangent:\n\nWe find the equation of the tangent as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-\\frac{7}{4} & =\\sqrt{3}(x-\\frac{7\\sqrt{3}}{4}) \\\\ y-\\frac{7}{4} & =\\sqrt{3}x-\\frac{21}{4} \\\\ y & =\\sqrt{3}\\,x-\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/4d/4d58fd3550e70915f3bc2a5e8ecd64cc4ef6c154a84ca536a5ca6ef6ddf49450.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2b01fc71-15e0-5989-a945-a229e3e4981a" "answer-field-ea70e8a0-cc70-507c-a9ef-fbc409c64de9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2b01fc71-15e0-5989-a945-a229e3e4981a" :answer-field/id #uuid "2b01fc71-15e0-5989-a945-a229e3e4981a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-15a44896-e16c-55e0-b031-ed3c4525e491" :answer-field/choices ["answer-15a44896-e16c-55e0-b031-ed3c4525e491"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15a44896-e16c-55e0-b031-ed3c4525e491" :answer/id #uuid "15a44896-e16c-55e0-b031-ed3c4525e491" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ea70e8a0-cc70-507c-a9ef-fbc409c64de9" :answer-field/id #uuid "ea70e8a0-cc70-507c-a9ef-fbc409c64de9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-441f08b4-04dd-5e42-838c-9e7b01251fc4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-441f08b4-04dd-5e42-838c-9e7b01251fc4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-441f08b4-04dd-5e42-838c-9e7b01251fc4" :answer/id #uuid "441f08b4-04dd-5e42-838c-9e7b01251fc4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-be4431be-3fe9-5dd2-82ee-71868596c05f" :question/id #uuid "be4431be-3fe9-5dd2-82ee-71868596c05f" :question/math-academy-id "q-103815" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent line to the polar curve $r={e}^{-\\theta }$ at $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(\\theta )={e}^{-\\theta }(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ),\\,{x}^{′}(\\theta )=-{e}^{-\\theta }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the equation of the tangent line to a polar curve at a point $P,$ we follow four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Calculate the derivative $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}:$\n\nIn this case, we're given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(\\theta )={e}^{-\\theta }(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ),\\,{x}^{′}(\\theta )=-{e}^{-\\theta }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{y}^{′}(\\theta )}{{x}^{′}(\\theta )} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-\\theta }(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}{{e}^{-\\theta }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\cancel{{e}^{-\\theta }}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}{\\cancel{{e}^{-\\theta }}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find the slope of the tangent at $P:$\n\nThe slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{\\theta =\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}))}{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}))} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})}{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Find the Cartesian coordinates of $P:$\n\nWe compute the $xy$-coordinates of $P$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={e}^{-\\theta }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={e}^{-\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{e}^{-\\pi /4} \\\\ {y}_{1} & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={e}^{-\\theta }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={e}^{-\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{e}^{-\\pi /4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of $P$ are $(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{e}^{-\\pi /4},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{e}^{-\\pi /4}).$\n\n**Step 4**: Using point-slope form, find the equation of the tangent:\n\nWe find the equation of the tangent as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{e}^{-\\pi /4} & =0\\cdot (x-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{e}^{-\\pi /4}) \\\\ y-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{e}^{-\\pi /4} & =0 \\\\ y & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{e}^{-\\pi /4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/6b/6b8602110483fcc09d9ac0c04a16ab4e624f00a2ff752851e9c027bef5c9bc83.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-099ae849-575f-5a4b-9f92-63b55d7f04a7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-099ae849-575f-5a4b-9f92-63b55d7f04a7" :answer-field/id #uuid "099ae849-575f-5a4b-9f92-63b55d7f04a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bf5c497b-6bdc-534b-b9f6-c27062181e55" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c5e096ad-fe8e-5767-ba62-fa5fd8b382c2" "answer-bf5c497b-6bdc-534b-b9f6-c27062181e55" "answer-c4b36070-55de-58e5-8e82-45b02bf82b34" "answer-acc71f80-e83e-56bd-a43b-28c93a53e550" "answer-dfa1dbde-f325-5791-9cf0-8c99ff494b8b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5e096ad-fe8e-5767-ba62-fa5fd8b382c2" :answer/id #uuid "c5e096ad-fe8e-5767-ba62-fa5fd8b382c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-x-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{e}^{-\\pi /4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bf5c497b-6bdc-534b-b9f6-c27062181e55" :answer/id #uuid "bf5c497b-6bdc-534b-b9f6-c27062181e55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{e}^{-\\pi /4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4b36070-55de-58e5-8e82-45b02bf82b34" :answer/id #uuid "c4b36070-55de-58e5-8e82-45b02bf82b34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{e}^{-\\pi /4}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-acc71f80-e83e-56bd-a43b-28c93a53e550" :answer/id #uuid "acc71f80-e83e-56bd-a43b-28c93a53e550" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{e}^{-\\pi /4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dfa1dbde-f325-5791-9cf0-8c99ff494b8b" :answer/id #uuid "dfa1dbde-f325-5791-9cf0-8c99ff494b8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{e}^{-\\pi /4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c7a90aa7-52b9-549e-8c2d-341971525e44" :question/id #uuid "c7a90aa7-52b9-549e-8c2d-341971525e44" :question/math-academy-id "q-141419" :question/problem "Find the equation of the **normal** line to the polar curve $r=1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ at $\\theta =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ given that\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(\\theta )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ),\\,{x}^{′}(\\theta )=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the equation of the normal line to a polar curve at a point $P,$ we follow four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Calculate the derivative $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}:$\n\nIn this case, we're given that\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(\\theta )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ),\\,{x}^{′}(\\theta )=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{y}^{′}(\\theta )}{{x}^{′}(\\theta )} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find the slope of the tangent at $P:$\n\nThe slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{\\theta =2\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{2\\pi }{3})}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{2\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{3})}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{-\\frac{1}{2}-2\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})}{2\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2})}{(-\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2})} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Find the Cartesian coordinates of $P:$\n\nWe compute the $xy$-coordinates of $P$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =(1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =(1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}))\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =(1-2(-\\frac{1}{2}))(-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-1 \\\\ {y}_{1} & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =(1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =(1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}))\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =(1-2(-\\frac{1}{2}))\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of $P$ are $(-1,\\sqrt{3}).$\n\n**Step 4**: Using point-slope form, find the equation of the normal:\n\nWe find the equation of the normal as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =-\\frac{1}{m}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-\\sqrt{3} & =3\\sqrt{3}\\cdot (x-(-1)) \\\\ y-\\sqrt{3} & =3\\sqrt{3}x+3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ y & =3\\sqrt{3}x+4\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/ba/ba0b04158944bd15aeea3220d4aa63321dd39c423a4f6646ba59c299fa8ef736.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fa2a0e8c-7f88-5fbd-86b3-0d022972fd45"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fa2a0e8c-7f88-5fbd-86b3-0d022972fd45" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa2a0e8c-7f88-5fbd-86b3-0d022972fd45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e8050d30-bcad-51d5-8a1a-40058eb95f05" :answer-field/choices ["answer-89c62352-327c-574f-9565-b27be34bf0f9" "answer-02fdcad9-364a-5070-981d-f9c1b4551dfc" "answer-e8050d30-bcad-51d5-8a1a-40058eb95f05" "answer-c725779e-c768-516a-9762-dfbab4f6c814" "answer-61f54b36-6f68-535c-92ab-0bc07509609f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-89c62352-327c-574f-9565-b27be34bf0f9" :answer/id #uuid "89c62352-327c-574f-9565-b27be34bf0f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-3\\sqrt{3}x-4\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-02fdcad9-364a-5070-981d-f9c1b4551dfc" :answer/id #uuid "02fdcad9-364a-5070-981d-f9c1b4551dfc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-4\\sqrt{3}x+3\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8050d30-bcad-51d5-8a1a-40058eb95f05" :answer/id #uuid "e8050d30-bcad-51d5-8a1a-40058eb95f05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=3\\sqrt{3}x+4\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c725779e-c768-516a-9762-dfbab4f6c814" :answer/id #uuid "c725779e-c768-516a-9762-dfbab4f6c814" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=3\\sqrt{3}x-4\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61f54b36-6f68-535c-92ab-0bc07509609f" :answer/id #uuid "61f54b36-6f68-535c-92ab-0bc07509609f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=4\\sqrt{3}x+3\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c83da1a3-053f-5553-bc32-57bdb774a02e" :question/id #uuid "c83da1a3-053f-5553-bc32-57bdb774a02e" :question/math-academy-id "q-351547" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the normal line to the polar curve $r=4\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ at $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(\\theta )=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )+4\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ), \\\\ {x}^{′}(\\theta )=2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )-4\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of the normal line is $y=$\n{{field-1}} $x\\,+$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the equation of the normal line to a polar curve at a point $P,$ we follow four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Calculate the derivative $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}:$\n\nIn this case, we're given that\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(\\theta )=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )+4\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ),\\,{x}^{′}(\\theta )=2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )-4\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{y}^{′}(\\theta )}{{x}^{′}(\\theta )} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )+4\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )}{2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )-4\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find the slope of the tangent at $P:$\n\nThe slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{\\theta =\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})+4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})}{2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})-4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2-\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Find the Cartesian coordinates of $P:$\n\nWe compute the $xy$-coordinates of $P$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =4\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\pi \\cdot {(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\ {y}_{1} & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =4\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of $P$ are $(\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$\n\n**Step 4**: Using point-slope form, find the equation of the normal:\n\nWe find the equation of the normal as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =-\\frac{1}{m}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-\\frac{\\pi }{2} & =\\frac{\\pi -2}{2}(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\ y & =\\frac{\\pi -2}{2}\\,x+\\frac{\\pi (4-\\pi )}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/2b/2bb2678804e79eb60cf9e1b16df60b8dad4ec4ccf8b2a9234a838c394ab9f3ac.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-da69ddf7-0c95-5610-bb80-afdff6c65e1a" "answer-field-eb8b6806-7bed-5b6d-a52c-5d124c4f7580"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-da69ddf7-0c95-5610-bb80-afdff6c65e1a" :answer-field/id #uuid "da69ddf7-0c95-5610-bb80-afdff6c65e1a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-a6726d53-1c49-55d4-a9fc-abfb02d98019" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a6726d53-1c49-55d4-a9fc-abfb02d98019"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6726d53-1c49-55d4-a9fc-abfb02d98019" :answer/id #uuid "a6726d53-1c49-55d4-a9fc-abfb02d98019" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi -2}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-eb8b6806-7bed-5b6d-a52c-5d124c4f7580" :answer-field/id #uuid "eb8b6806-7bed-5b6d-a52c-5d124c4f7580" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-bae7493b-97fa-5e69-b993-6f9d41cd3185" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bae7493b-97fa-5e69-b993-6f9d41cd3185"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bae7493b-97fa-5e69-b993-6f9d41cd3185" :answer/id #uuid "bae7493b-97fa-5e69-b993-6f9d41cd3185" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi (4-\\pi )}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4bd1b924-fea7-5666-9b66-85d3682d3092" :question/id #uuid "4bd1b924-fea7-5666-9b66-85d3682d3092" :question/math-academy-id "q-362903" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation $y=f(x)$ of the normal line to the polar curve $r=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ at $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2\\theta ).\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of the normal line is $y=$\n{{field-1}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the equation of the normal line to a polar curve at a point $P,$ we follow four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Calculate the derivative $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}:$\n\nIn this case, we're given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2\\theta ).\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find the slope of the tangent at $P:$\n\nThe slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{\\theta =\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Find the Cartesian coordinates of $P:$\n\nWe compute the $xy$-coordinates of $P$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3} \\\\ {y}_{1} & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of $P$ are $(\\sqrt{3},1).$\n\n**Step 4**: Using point-slope form, find the equation of the normal:\n\nWe find the equation of the normal as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =-\\frac{1}{m}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}(x-\\sqrt{3}) \\\\ y-1 & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}x+1 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\,x+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/b2/b2485a1b1386468904947c52ff3f52997f72597da84384ae41d246f386a39232.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c603d277-c436-515e-9401-4e14d4e32737" "answer-field-9960e886-6591-52e7-b6de-f3f58994bcca"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c603d277-c436-515e-9401-4e14d4e32737" :answer-field/id #uuid "c603d277-c436-515e-9401-4e14d4e32737" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-9d4234aa-c19a-50c4-8afe-1f256cd2c1dc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9d4234aa-c19a-50c4-8afe-1f256cd2c1dc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d4234aa-c19a-50c4-8afe-1f256cd2c1dc" :answer/id #uuid "9d4234aa-c19a-50c4-8afe-1f256cd2c1dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9960e886-6591-52e7-b6de-f3f58994bcca" :answer-field/id #uuid "9960e886-6591-52e7-b6de-f3f58994bcca" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-cf16f7e4-17c9-549f-a864-943b15c55740" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cf16f7e4-17c9-549f-a864-943b15c55740"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf16f7e4-17c9-549f-a864-943b15c55740" :answer/id #uuid "cf16f7e4-17c9-549f-a864-943b15c55740" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4b160342-1c9b-5cb6-9f7b-8bf55c5af2c6" :question/id #uuid "4b160342-1c9b-5cb6-9f7b-8bf55c5af2c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-141356" :question/problem "Find the equation of the **normal** line to the polar curve $r={\\theta }^{2}$ at $\\theta =\\frac{3\\pi }{2},$ given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the equation of the normal line to a polar curve at a point $P,$ we follow four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Calculate the derivative $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}:$\n\nIn this case, we're given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }.\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find the slope of the tangent at $P:$\n\nThe slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{\\theta =3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})+\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}))}{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}))} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot (-1)+\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\cdot 0}{(2\\cdot 0-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\cdot (-1))} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Find the Cartesian coordinates of $P:$\n\nWe compute the $xy$-coordinates of $P$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\theta }^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})}^{2}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0 \\\\ {y}_{1} & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\theta }^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})}^{2}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of $P$ are $(0,-\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}).$\n\n**Step 4**: Using point-slope form, find the equation of the normal:\n\nWe find the equation of the normal as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =-\\frac{1}{m}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}) & =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}\\cdot (x-0) \\\\ y+\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4} & =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}\\,x \\\\ y & =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}x-\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/8f/8f39669eaedc42a26d28d96f6dbb961080816e7fadd182b79a260c8de27b3d1a.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ea5f0102-7a6b-5740-bb7e-b8c83d6d91f6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ea5f0102-7a6b-5740-bb7e-b8c83d6d91f6" :answer-field/id #uuid "ea5f0102-7a6b-5740-bb7e-b8c83d6d91f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bd150fa0-ce1f-5591-a343-840beb560c4e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-08ad0bb0-44b4-5377-b18a-d503eaa1b661" "answer-2399beaf-eace-5a34-9002-6ad316000d27" "answer-f8ccf14d-454f-5062-8149-cc1e7174890e" "answer-ff8ca8d0-5bd2-5279-a5a0-2e48e66c5361" "answer-bd150fa0-ce1f-5591-a343-840beb560c4e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-08ad0bb0-44b4-5377-b18a-d503eaa1b661" :answer/id #uuid "08ad0bb0-44b4-5377-b18a-d503eaa1b661" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}x-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2399beaf-eace-5a34-9002-6ad316000d27" :answer/id #uuid "2399beaf-eace-5a34-9002-6ad316000d27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}x-\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f8ccf14d-454f-5062-8149-cc1e7174890e" :answer/id #uuid "f8ccf14d-454f-5062-8149-cc1e7174890e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}x-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff8ca8d0-5bd2-5279-a5a0-2e48e66c5361" :answer/id #uuid "ff8ca8d0-5bd2-5279-a5a0-2e48e66c5361" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}x-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd150fa0-ce1f-5591-a343-840beb560c4e" :answer/id #uuid "bd150fa0-ce1f-5591-a343-840beb560c4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}x-\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184437 :question/problem "Find the equation of the **normal** line to the polar curve $r=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )$ at $\\theta =\\frac{3\\pi }{4},$ given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the equation of the normal line to a polar curve at a point $P,$ we follow four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Calculate the derivative $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}:$\n\nIn this case, we're given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }.\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find the slope of the tangent at $P:$\n\nThe slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{\\theta =3\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{9\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}))}{(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{9\\pi }{4})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}))} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})}{(\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}+(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}))} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{2})}{(\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{2})} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Find the Cartesian coordinates of $P:$\n\nWe compute the $xy$-coordinates of $P$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ {y}_{1} & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of $P$ are $(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}).$\n\n**Step 4**: Using point-slope form, find the equation of the normal:\n\nWe find the equation of the normal as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =-\\frac{1}{m}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) & =-1\\cdot (x-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\ y+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & =-x+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ y & =-x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/31/3185d528869c760d55d5f01aebae58ef41c6c325c7a3cb56d67c401ecfb80b2b.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180799 :answer-field/correct "answer-6a904a99-9555-59da-b4b7-d0e6556359cc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-96221e88-2457-5022-8d30-9d942b87da36" "answer-6a904a99-9555-59da-b4b7-d0e6556359cc" "answer-c63bb719-501d-5899-9990-749d6453007b" "answer-1cb26523-cf9a-5e6f-a6df-561191311046" "answer-82b05dd1-ec82-5b6d-87ab-194bbf6fb236"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-96221e88-2457-5022-8d30-9d942b87da36" :answer/id #uuid "96221e88-2457-5022-8d30-9d942b87da36" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\sqrt{2}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a904a99-9555-59da-b4b7-d0e6556359cc" :answer/id #uuid "6a904a99-9555-59da-b4b7-d0e6556359cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c63bb719-501d-5899-9990-749d6453007b" :answer/id #uuid "c63bb719-501d-5899-9990-749d6453007b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-x+\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1cb26523-cf9a-5e6f-a6df-561191311046" :answer/id #uuid "1cb26523-cf9a-5e6f-a6df-561191311046" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x+\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82b05dd1-ec82-5b6d-87ab-194bbf6fb236" :answer/id #uuid "82b05dd1-ec82-5b6d-87ab-194bbf6fb236" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x-\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186185342 :tutorial/content "![](images/a0/a0b4ad67ea80f6d6eec3a15b3df18d551d84263c7424405588bd15162ef4e7c2.png)\n\nThe polar curve shown above is defined as\n\n$$\nr(\\theta) = 4 - 3\\cos \\theta, \\qquad 0\\leq \\theta < 2\\pi.\n$$\n\nWe have $\\theta = \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$ at the point $P.$ The tangent to the curve at $P$ is shown in the diagram. \n\nTo find the equation of the tangent line to the curve at $P,$ we follow four steps.\n\n**Step 1**: Calculate the derivative $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}.$\n\nUsing techniques that we've previously discussed, we can show that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(\\theta )=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ,\\,{x}^{′}(\\theta )=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta -4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can find $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{y}^{′}(\\theta )}{{x}^{′}(\\theta )} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta -4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find the slope of the tangent at $P.$\n\nThe slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{\\theta =\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})}{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )}{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+3}{0-4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Find the Cartesian coordinates of $P.$\n\nWe compute the $xy$-coordinates of $P$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =(4-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =(4-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =0 \\\\ {y}_{1} & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =(4-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =(4-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of $P$ are $\\left( 0, 4 \\right).$\n\n**Step 4**: Using point-slope form, find the equation of the tangent.\n\nWe find the equation of the tangent as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-4 & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot (x-0) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{3}{4}x+4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184419 :activity/expected-seconds 1260.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186185006 :step/math-academy-id 642668 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184944 :step/math-academy-id 642669 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186185001 :step/math-academy-id 642672 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186062533 :answer-field/choices 17592186062534] [:db/retract 17592186062533 :answer-field/choices 17592186062535] [:db/retract 17592186062533 :answer-field/choices 17592186062536] [:db/retract 17592186062533 :answer-field/choices 17592186062537] [:db/retract 17592186062533 :answer-field/choices 17592186062538] {:db/id 17592186064222 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6c864496-70bc-5f2d-82d0-559a3bc9072f" "question-9ddda73a-66ad-5c78-97bd-db73c90fdc26"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-6c864496-70bc-5f2d-82d0-559a3bc9072f" :question/id #uuid "6c864496-70bc-5f2d-82d0-559a3bc9072f" :question/math-academy-id "q-100186" :question/problem "Simplify $(-32)^{0}.$" :question/worked-solution "Any number raised to the power of zero is equal to $1.$ So, \n\n$$\n(-32)^{0}=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cccbddba-c813-58ff-9619-9ede97166f31"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cccbddba-c813-58ff-9619-9ede97166f31" :answer-field/id #uuid "cccbddba-c813-58ff-9619-9ede97166f31" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1a557119-a04d-5392-9590-db6f76a17677" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0bb75cad-69d3-58ee-902d-2f04ec5f09c5" "answer-6e41045a-a43e-5e74-a7e6-2a3baefd2866" "answer-8d699824-ccbe-55f1-8873-b9e9fbb3e86f" "answer-1a557119-a04d-5392-9590-db6f76a17677" "answer-9092158c-68be-5a62-8f08-860cc48b4867"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0bb75cad-69d3-58ee-902d-2f04ec5f09c5" :answer/id #uuid "0bb75cad-69d3-58ee-902d-2f04ec5f09c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e41045a-a43e-5e74-a7e6-2a3baefd2866" :answer/id #uuid "6e41045a-a43e-5e74-a7e6-2a3baefd2866" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d699824-ccbe-55f1-8873-b9e9fbb3e86f" :answer/id #uuid "8d699824-ccbe-55f1-8873-b9e9fbb3e86f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a557119-a04d-5392-9590-db6f76a17677" :answer/id #uuid "1a557119-a04d-5392-9590-db6f76a17677" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9092158c-68be-5a62-8f08-860cc48b4867" :answer/id #uuid "9092158c-68be-5a62-8f08-860cc48b4867" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Undefined" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133963 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5270a65a-9011-5c4a-8ec5-b8423546a5ab"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-5270a65a-9011-5c4a-8ec5-b8423546a5ab" :question/id #uuid "5270a65a-9011-5c4a-8ec5-b8423546a5ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-70119" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\frac{3(2x-4)}{4(5-x)}$ for $x=6.$" :question/worked-solution "We replace $x$ with $6$ in the expression and simplify as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3(2x-4)}{4(5-x)} & = \\\\ \\frac{3(2(6)-4)}{4(5-6)} & = \\\\ \\frac{3(8)}{4(-1)} & = \\\\ \\frac{24}{-4} & = \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3ef3b252-7a41-5683-98fb-90a69fdfa0b1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3ef3b252-7a41-5683-98fb-90a69fdfa0b1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3ef3b252-7a41-5683-98fb-90a69fdfa0b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-63083205-3b2c-5bcd-81e6-ff997c6c0c5d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c3a6cdb5-bb1f-5d2a-a186-55d7223adb10" "answer-63083205-3b2c-5bcd-81e6-ff997c6c0c5d" "answer-9dd8f733-31e8-5469-a772-f0c2bce876e9" "answer-4f03e8ba-15b1-5ceb-9f37-91bebc4eb5aa" "answer-ec996c53-a1e7-585d-b640-0dfebe682167"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3a6cdb5-bb1f-5d2a-a186-55d7223adb10" :answer/id #uuid "c3a6cdb5-bb1f-5d2a-a186-55d7223adb10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-63083205-3b2c-5bcd-81e6-ff997c6c0c5d" :answer/id #uuid "63083205-3b2c-5bcd-81e6-ff997c6c0c5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9dd8f733-31e8-5469-a772-f0c2bce876e9" :answer/id #uuid "9dd8f733-31e8-5469-a772-f0c2bce876e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4f03e8ba-15b1-5ceb-9f37-91bebc4eb5aa" :answer/id #uuid "4f03e8ba-15b1-5ceb-9f37-91bebc4eb5aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec996c53-a1e7-585d-b640-0dfebe682167" :answer/id #uuid "ec996c53-a1e7-585d-b640-0dfebe682167" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186138511 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-49e631ed-e489-57e1-8328-8ad962002fdf"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-49e631ed-e489-57e1-8328-8ad962002fdf" :question/id #uuid "49e631ed-e489-57e1-8328-8ad962002fdf" :question/math-academy-id "q-75382" :question/problem "$3+\\frac{3}{2}x-1-\\frac{7}{4}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We collect and combine the like terms, simplifying the coefficients as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3+\\frac{3x}{2}-1-\\frac{7x}{4} & = \\\\ (\\frac{3x}{2}-\\frac{7x}{4})+(3-1) & = \\\\ (\\frac{6}{4}-\\frac{7}{4})x+(3-1) & = \\\\ (\\frac{6-7}{4})x+2 & = \\\\ -\\frac{1}{4}x+2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-41165c67-5f21-5f55-b678-99fd5befca9d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-41165c67-5f21-5f55-b678-99fd5befca9d" :answer-field/id #uuid "41165c67-5f21-5f55-b678-99fd5befca9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0aa4e6a0-3aeb-559f-96d7-bd92f700b296" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0aa4e6a0-3aeb-559f-96d7-bd92f700b296" "answer-fe0f995b-cc21-5f36-9851-e5fb6941662d" "answer-b490045f-fa26-53d0-83e1-8ad88e404827" "answer-fdae0bda-2f60-5c1b-bf1e-e3f18a773891" "answer-b7410f52-b281-5541-8a42-cabcaa3e3486"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0aa4e6a0-3aeb-559f-96d7-bd92f700b296" :answer/id #uuid "0aa4e6a0-3aeb-559f-96d7-bd92f700b296" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}x+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fe0f995b-cc21-5f36-9851-e5fb6941662d" :answer/id #uuid "fe0f995b-cc21-5f36-9851-e5fb6941662d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b490045f-fa26-53d0-83e1-8ad88e404827" :answer/id #uuid "b490045f-fa26-53d0-83e1-8ad88e404827" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}x+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fdae0bda-2f60-5c1b-bf1e-e3f18a773891" :answer/id #uuid "fdae0bda-2f60-5c1b-bf1e-e3f18a773891" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}x-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b7410f52-b281-5541-8a42-cabcaa3e3486" :answer/id #uuid "b7410f52-b281-5541-8a42-cabcaa3e3486" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}x+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134342 :question/problem "Evaluate $\\sqrt{7x-4}$ for $x=7.$" :question/worked-solution "We replace $x$ with $7$ in the given expression, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{7x-4} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{7\\cdot 7-4} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{49-4} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{45}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify even further using the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{45} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{9\\cdot 5} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{3}^{2}\\cdot 5} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{3}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{5} & = \\\\ 3\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186132091 :answer-field/correct 17592186132093 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064746 :question/problem "Factor ${x}^{2}+18x+81.$" :question/worked-solution "The \"square of a sum\" formula states that\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2ax+{a}^{2}=(x+a)^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe will use this formula to factor the given trinomial. Our trinomial is\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+18x+81.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write the constant term as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+18x+{9}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we factor a $2$ out of the linear term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2\\cdot 9x+{9}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we factor the trinomial using the square of sum formula with $a=9.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+9)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186062533 :answer-field/correct "answer-b4dc61be-f756-58b1-a8f4-a638c0bed511" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3a1ce303-f436-5ddb-8e1d-0041ee4f763d" "answer-5d507733-ce93-5b3b-900f-5ffc45f84dab" "answer-b4dc61be-f756-58b1-a8f4-a638c0bed511" "answer-3688d49a-8533-5c2a-bb88-92312001ffa2" "answer-af7a1ec4-cf1a-56ea-b663-65069724d8bf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3a1ce303-f436-5ddb-8e1d-0041ee4f763d" :answer/id #uuid "3a1ce303-f436-5ddb-8e1d-0041ee4f763d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5d507733-ce93-5b3b-900f-5ffc45f84dab" :answer/id #uuid "5d507733-ce93-5b3b-900f-5ffc45f84dab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+81)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4dc61be-f756-58b1-a8f4-a638c0bed511" :answer/id #uuid "b4dc61be-f756-58b1-a8f4-a638c0bed511" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+9)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3688d49a-8533-5c2a-bb88-92312001ffa2" :answer/id #uuid "3688d49a-8533-5c2a-bb88-92312001ffa2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(x+6)}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af7a1ec4-cf1a-56ea-b663-65069724d8bf" :answer/id #uuid "af7a1ec4-cf1a-56ea-b663-65069724d8bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(x-9)}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064243 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3c104695-c936-5d0f-b4ab-74c8ede24e1a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-3c104695-c936-5d0f-b4ab-74c8ede24e1a" :question/id #uuid "3c104695-c936-5d0f-b4ab-74c8ede24e1a" :question/math-academy-id "q-61969" :question/problem "$(x-3y)({x}^{2}+4y)=$" :question/worked-solution "We take each term of the first binomial and multiply it by the second binomial. Then, we simplify by collecting like terms.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3y)({x}^{2}+4y) & = \\\\ x({x}^{2}+4y)-3y({x}^{2}+4y) & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+4xy-3{x}^{2}y-12{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe cannot simplify the above expression any further because there are no like terms." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ca8079df-5f8f-5314-942f-74ff8f9992ad"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ca8079df-5f8f-5314-942f-74ff8f9992ad" :answer-field/id #uuid "ca8079df-5f8f-5314-942f-74ff8f9992ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-93caafae-8ef1-5347-b1d8-6a4a383a7b02" :answer-field/choices ["answer-13222a6f-012f-5b93-a152-dcbb407a165a" "answer-83e3ff62-308c-5bca-b296-5156cbfaf36a" "answer-64919853-e1e4-5b77-bdc8-8edcf53889dc" "answer-93caafae-8ef1-5347-b1d8-6a4a383a7b02" "answer-bbda9460-e5ed-5f4f-8e0b-ba7b20413496"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-13222a6f-012f-5b93-a152-dcbb407a165a" :answer/id #uuid "13222a6f-012f-5b93-a152-dcbb407a165a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{3}+12{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83e3ff62-308c-5bca-b296-5156cbfaf36a" :answer/id #uuid "83e3ff62-308c-5bca-b296-5156cbfaf36a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{3}+4xy+3{x}^{2}y+12{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-64919853-e1e4-5b77-bdc8-8edcf53889dc" :answer/id #uuid "64919853-e1e4-5b77-bdc8-8edcf53889dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{3}+4xy-3{x}^{2}y+12{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-93caafae-8ef1-5347-b1d8-6a4a383a7b02" :answer/id #uuid "93caafae-8ef1-5347-b1d8-6a4a383a7b02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{3}+4xy-3{x}^{2}y-12{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bbda9460-e5ed-5f4f-8e0b-ba7b20413496" :answer/id #uuid "bbda9460-e5ed-5f4f-8e0b-ba7b20413496" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{3}-12{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059827 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-eee859cf-032a-5a34-a81e-4f392e60f1ec"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-eee859cf-032a-5a34-a81e-4f392e60f1ec" :question/id #uuid "eee859cf-032a-5a34-a81e-4f392e60f1ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-102205" :question/problem "The inequality $0<x\\le 7$ can be expressed in interval notation as" :question/worked-solution "Every inequality can be expressed as an interval. We use the following notations:\n\n- Parentheses $()$ if the endpoints are *not* included.\n\n- Brackets $[]$ if the endpoints *are* included.\n\nFor the given inequality \n\n$$\n0\\,\\,<\\,\\,x\\,\\,\\le \\,\\,7\n$$\n\nwe note the following:\n\n- The left endpoint $0$ is *not* included in the interval. Therefore, we use $(\\,.$\n\n- The right endpoint $7$ *is* included in the interval. Therefore, we use $]\\,.$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding interval is\n\n$$\nx\\in (0,7].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2e9148e1-c517-584b-81ce-f179a876160f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2e9148e1-c517-584b-81ce-f179a876160f" :answer-field/id #uuid "2e9148e1-c517-584b-81ce-f179a876160f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-60ed0177-10a3-5141-8f0d-6b2603ad36d8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d20e5b5b-a9db-58d3-92e2-e77645249c59" "answer-60ed0177-10a3-5141-8f0d-6b2603ad36d8" "answer-a7f3d4df-e271-59b6-b3ae-010d04a7214b" "answer-eb83e406-5d7f-5868-bb88-3e5884a89c66" "answer-487f9cd5-aca0-5110-a351-1c3d45518748"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d20e5b5b-a9db-58d3-92e2-e77645249c59" :answer/id #uuid "d20e5b5b-a9db-58d3-92e2-e77645249c59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (0,7)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60ed0177-10a3-5141-8f0d-6b2603ad36d8" :answer/id #uuid "60ed0177-10a3-5141-8f0d-6b2603ad36d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (0,7]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7f3d4df-e271-59b6-b3ae-010d04a7214b" :answer/id #uuid "a7f3d4df-e271-59b6-b3ae-010d04a7214b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in [-7,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb83e406-5d7f-5868-bb88-3e5884a89c66" :answer/id #uuid "eb83e406-5d7f-5868-bb88-3e5884a89c66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in [0,7)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-487f9cd5-aca0-5110-a351-1c3d45518748" :answer/id #uuid "487f9cd5-aca0-5110-a351-1c3d45518748" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in [0,7]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054836 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-651d48b6-dcdd-5bc2-87b4-a66ffecf04ac"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-651d48b6-dcdd-5bc2-87b4-a66ffecf04ac" :question/id #uuid "651d48b6-dcdd-5bc2-87b4-a66ffecf04ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-175589" :question/problem "If $\\frac{1}{15}=-\\frac{m}{3},$ then $m=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's swap the left and right-hand sides so that the variable is on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n-\\frac{m}{3}=\\frac{1}{15}\n$$\n\nThen, we remove the negative sign from the variable. To do this, we multiply both sides of the equation by $-1.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{m}{3} & =\\frac{1}{15} \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-\\frac{m}{3}) & =(-1)\\cdot \\frac{1}{15} \\\\ \\frac{m}{3} & =-\\frac{1}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the equation above, $m$ is being divided by $3.$ To isolate $m$, we can perform the opposite operation, which is *multiplying* by $3.$ So, we multiply both sides of the equation by $3$ and simplify.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{m}{3} & =-\\frac{1}{15} \\\\ 3\\cdot \\frac{m}{3} & =3\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{15}) \\\\ \\frac{3m}{3} & =-\\frac{3}{15} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{3}m}{\\cancel{3}} & =-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ m & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3f4ee068-a4ba-5955-9803-7974762ed968"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3f4ee068-a4ba-5955-9803-7974762ed968" :answer-field/id #uuid "3f4ee068-a4ba-5955-9803-7974762ed968" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-f7af24af-4c8d-5f43-b558-8db7ccd96709" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f7af24af-4c8d-5f43-b558-8db7ccd96709"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7af24af-4c8d-5f43-b558-8db7ccd96709" :answer/id #uuid "f7af24af-4c8d-5f43-b558-8db7ccd96709" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073884 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6ca180bb-426b-5acf-99a3-c4512087f7c5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-6ca180bb-426b-5acf-99a3-c4512087f7c5" :question/id #uuid "6ca180bb-426b-5acf-99a3-c4512087f7c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-64174" :question/problem "![](images/2d/2d3fc4b568492c8435f72c28010c21b0c0746e2abe46922fdb942eaba5cf8b05.png)\n\nWhat $x:y$ ratio is shown in the graph above?" :question/worked-solution "We see that the point $(7,5)$ lies on the graph. Let's write the ratio $7:5$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{5}\n$$\n\nWe can not simplify this fraction further. Hence, we can say that the graph shows the ratio $7:5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fa9c72a6-010c-59fe-8341-86fe3d0c838b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fa9c72a6-010c-59fe-8341-86fe3d0c838b" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa9c72a6-010c-59fe-8341-86fe3d0c838b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a2846c32-c82b-5b7d-b57a-377fe83617dc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6164133d-ab71-544e-b707-ee1cdfd93d9c" "answer-c2a8b31e-f9b4-5ed6-bd93-9574693c1c7e" "answer-5fab75dc-4f3e-52db-a0cc-5aaa48d05e73" "answer-8c43a522-e9ee-5ff5-955f-7fa9936b8815" "answer-a2846c32-c82b-5b7d-b57a-377fe83617dc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6164133d-ab71-544e-b707-ee1cdfd93d9c" :answer/id #uuid "6164133d-ab71-544e-b707-ee1cdfd93d9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12:7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c2a8b31e-f9b4-5ed6-bd93-9574693c1c7e" :answer/id #uuid "c2a8b31e-f9b4-5ed6-bd93-9574693c1c7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4:3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5fab75dc-4f3e-52db-a0cc-5aaa48d05e73" :answer/id #uuid "5fab75dc-4f3e-52db-a0cc-5aaa48d05e73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5:2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c43a522-e9ee-5ff5-955f-7fa9936b8815" :answer/id #uuid "8c43a522-e9ee-5ff5-955f-7fa9936b8815" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5:7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2846c32-c82b-5b7d-b57a-377fe83617dc" :answer/id #uuid "a2846c32-c82b-5b7d-b57a-377fe83617dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7:5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152296 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-16908ce6-e741-598e-9537-76866b0601d0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-16908ce6-e741-598e-9537-76866b0601d0" :question/id #uuid "16908ce6-e741-598e-9537-76866b0601d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-326520" :question/problem "A backpack costs $$64$ before tax. If a $7.75%$ sales tax is applied, what is the total price after tax?" :question/worked-solution "To find the total price after tax, we apply a $7.75%$ increase to the original price.\n\nIncreasing by $7.75%$ means that we must apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+7.75%=107.75%=1.0775\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the original price by $1.0775:$\n\n$$\n64\\times 1.0775=68.96.\n$$\n\nSo, the total price of the backpack after tax is $$68.96.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-471f8877-1cd7-5a08-8ddd-83f1e22878b3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-471f8877-1cd7-5a08-8ddd-83f1e22878b3" :answer-field/id #uuid "471f8877-1cd7-5a08-8ddd-83f1e22878b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-52d1a82b-37fe-5eb7-b559-3be5ae2a38d5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e7964137-d215-566b-8387-07ced5b59223" "answer-52d1a82b-37fe-5eb7-b559-3be5ae2a38d5" "answer-be402325-f576-53ec-ac7a-edffe8a73154" "answer-1ca874c1-4215-5fa3-9f9b-fc5a7fcfea4f" "answer-24b8c98f-8ea6-5177-8cce-121d4ea2ad13"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e7964137-d215-566b-8387-07ced5b59223" :answer/id #uuid "e7964137-d215-566b-8387-07ced5b59223" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$66.35$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-52d1a82b-37fe-5eb7-b559-3be5ae2a38d5" :answer/id #uuid "52d1a82b-37fe-5eb7-b559-3be5ae2a38d5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$68.96$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be402325-f576-53ec-ac7a-edffe8a73154" :answer/id #uuid "be402325-f576-53ec-ac7a-edffe8a73154" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$69.50$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1ca874c1-4215-5fa3-9f9b-fc5a7fcfea4f" :answer/id #uuid "1ca874c1-4215-5fa3-9f9b-fc5a7fcfea4f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$70.25$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-24b8c98f-8ea6-5177-8cce-121d4ea2ad13" :answer/id #uuid "24b8c98f-8ea6-5177-8cce-121d4ea2ad13" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$71.00$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186138753 :question/problem "The volume $v$ of acid in a test tube measures $10.25\\,\\text{mL}$ to the nearest hundredth of a milliliter. Determine the upper and lower bounds of this measurement.\n\n{{field-1}}$\\text{mL}$\n$\\,\\le v<$\n{{field-2}}$\\text{mL}$" :question/worked-solution "Our measurement is given to the nearest $0.01\\,\\text{mL}.$ So, the greatest possible error of this measurement is\n\n$$\n\\frac{0.01\\,\\text{mL}}{2}=0.005\\,\\text{mL}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the lower and upper bounds of this measurement as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{lower bound} & =10.25\\,\\text{mL}-0.005\\,\\text{mL} \\\\  & =10.245\\,\\text{mL} \\\\ \\text{upper bound} & =10.25\\,\\text{mL}+0.005\\,\\text{mL} \\\\  & =10.255\\,\\text{mL}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the exact value of $v$ lies between the lower and upper bound, we conclude that\n\n$$\n10.245\\,\\text{mL}\\le v<10.255\\,\\text{mL}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186135518 :answer-field/correct "answer-a1554ed6-8431-5d28-996f-2deb66c4b977" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a1554ed6-8431-5d28-996f-2deb66c4b977"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1554ed6-8431-5d28-996f-2deb66c4b977" :answer/id #uuid "a1554ed6-8431-5d28-996f-2deb66c4b977" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10.245" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186135517 :answer-field/correct "answer-be3c585c-88dd-5f80-a36b-2d6e93e57be1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-be3c585c-88dd-5f80-a36b-2d6e93e57be1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be3c585c-88dd-5f80-a36b-2d6e93e57be1" :answer/id #uuid "be3c585c-88dd-5f80-a36b-2d6e93e57be1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10.255" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054626 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9169a9eb-58fd-54ef-9fd7-4f2515dd156b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9169a9eb-58fd-54ef-9fd7-4f2515dd156b" :question/id #uuid "9169a9eb-58fd-54ef-9fd7-4f2515dd156b" :question/math-academy-id "q-215792" :question/problem "If $p=-1,$ then $|4p+1{|}^{3}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We substitute $p=-1$ and then evaluate the absolute value before we simplify the rest of the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|4p+1{|}^{3} & = \\\\ |4(-1)+1{|}^{3} & = \\\\ |-4+1{|}^{3} & = \\\\ |-3{|}^{3} & = \\\\ (3)^{3} & = \\\\ 27\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-575678ef-cc64-5787-8f72-c733f23afefd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-575678ef-cc64-5787-8f72-c733f23afefd" :answer-field/id #uuid "575678ef-cc64-5787-8f72-c733f23afefd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ff07cacd-7a6b-524d-9691-0f6ed1e2ea8a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ff07cacd-7a6b-524d-9691-0f6ed1e2ea8a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff07cacd-7a6b-524d-9691-0f6ed1e2ea8a" :answer/id #uuid "ff07cacd-7a6b-524d-9691-0f6ed1e2ea8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073820 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-69122235-d824-5d29-8715-1c0104966b58"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-69122235-d824-5d29-8715-1c0104966b58" :question/id #uuid "69122235-d824-5d29-8715-1c0104966b58" :question/math-academy-id "q-178632" :question/problem "The additive inverse of $24$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the additive inverse of the number $24$, we change its sign by placing a minus symbol $(-)$ in front of it. So, we obtain \n\n$$\n-\\,(24)=-24.\n$$\n\nTo check our work, we simply add the inverse to the original number. If we're correct, we should get zero.\n\n$$\n24+(-24)=24-24=0\\,✓\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b6427fee-9638-5bb5-9dd9-2d2aacd365d5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b6427fee-9638-5bb5-9dd9-2d2aacd365d5" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6427fee-9638-5bb5-9dd9-2d2aacd365d5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-92a411b8-db16-53b9-9023-1e2885ea56ad" :answer-field/choices ["answer-92a411b8-db16-53b9-9023-1e2885ea56ad"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92a411b