eb33bfa0360b9f9b34a0d49a1a2b237e6f35a12d53b266.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above shows the relationship between the number of t-shirts and the number of socks sold by a clothing store over several days.\nWhich of the following is the trend line of the scatter plot above?" :question/worked-solution "From the plot, it seems that the data points are scattered randomly. Therefore, there is no linear trend." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-eed8313f-5c67-58d4-a3c0-316ed731d674"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-eed8313f-5c67-58d4-a3c0-316ed731d674" :answer-field/id #uuid "eed8313f-5c67-58d4-a3c0-316ed731d674" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b19635d9-02c0-5c65-981e-cb9ab91408e1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6210732b-50a1-5a05-9e37-d1facd024c47" "answer-1da2cc1f-d065-58c9-a771-7cc8dc0674a1" "answer-d345c2be-76c7-50ff-98e9-3f12072b13a1" "answer-9c3a2f19-4a2f-50b0-ad51-3a6544cf7362" "answer-b19635d9-02c0-5c65-981e-cb9ab91408e1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6210732b-50a1-5a05-9e37-d1facd024c47" :answer/id #uuid "6210732b-50a1-5a05-9e37-d1facd024c47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1da2cc1f-d065-58c9-a771-7cc8dc0674a1" :answer/id #uuid "1da2cc1f-d065-58c9-a771-7cc8dc0674a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "q" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d345c2be-76c7-50ff-98e9-3f12072b13a1" :answer/id #uuid "d345c2be-76c7-50ff-98e9-3f12072b13a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9c3a2f19-4a2f-50b0-ad51-3a6544cf7362" :answer/id #uuid "9c3a2f19-4a2f-50b0-ad51-3a6544cf7362" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b19635d9-02c0-5c65-981e-cb9ab91408e1" :answer/id #uuid "b19635d9-02c0-5c65-981e-cb9ab91408e1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "There is no linear trend in the data" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-94bd2cbd-504c-548c-9ed1-5e5adaadef48" :question/id #uuid "94bd2cbd-504c-548c-9ed1-5e5adaadef48" :question/math-academy-id "q-134020" :question/problem "![](images/b8/b82ed81f724322dc05a2c65d3635ac74f5ca92ff413e9d7e5131ebb604269f26.png)\n\nDetermine the equation of the trend line shown above." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the trend line passes through the points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(-4,6)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(4,3).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-6}{4-(-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=-\\frac{3}{8}$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{3}{8}x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can find this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(-4,6):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{3}{8}x+b \\\\ 6 & =-\\frac{3}{8}(-4)+b \\\\ 6 & =\\frac{3}{2}+b \\\\ 12 & =3+2b \\\\ b & =\\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{3}{8}x+\\frac{9}{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3b9c6ec5-0c09-548c-8228-cf9708222788"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3b9c6ec5-0c09-548c-8228-cf9708222788" :answer-field/id #uuid "3b9c6ec5-0c09-548c-8228-cf9708222788" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2d252d8c-d493-5170-b7a6-d761bb5e5e7d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-44453f11-c660-507e-a6a0-3784729b906d" "answer-4fa23fc9-19ad-5907-93ad-4b1a0885d020" "answer-2d252d8c-d493-5170-b7a6-d761bb5e5e7d" "answer-c654e87c-750d-5151-96fc-24fd14b7437b" "answer-17356e8d-52ec-5267-88b4-0e420beef0c7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-44453f11-c660-507e-a6a0-3784729b906d" :answer/id #uuid "44453f11-c660-507e-a6a0-3784729b906d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{9}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4fa23fc9-19ad-5907-93ad-4b1a0885d020" :answer/id #uuid "4fa23fc9-19ad-5907-93ad-4b1a0885d020" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{3}{8}x+\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2d252d8c-d493-5170-b7a6-d761bb5e5e7d" :answer/id #uuid "2d252d8c-d493-5170-b7a6-d761bb5e5e7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{3}{8}x+\\frac{9}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c654e87c-750d-5151-96fc-24fd14b7437b" :answer/id #uuid "c654e87c-750d-5151-96fc-24fd14b7437b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{5}{8}x+\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17356e8d-52ec-5267-88b4-0e420beef0c7" :answer/id #uuid "17356e8d-52ec-5267-88b4-0e420beef0c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{5}{8}x+\\frac{9}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-38830f71-0f2a-562f-b716-243d080e51d3" :question/id #uuid "38830f71-0f2a-562f-b716-243d080e51d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-134012" :question/problem "![](images/60/60b546c0e2d37362fefde1023ed093d2f544b187742bb690d5fe60bc417b48d4.png)\n\nWhat is the slope of the trend line shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the trend line passes through the points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(1,2)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(3,5).$\n\nTherefore, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-2}{3-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-71b478d5-40d3-56c6-919f-e4aca770b60e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-71b478d5-40d3-56c6-919f-e4aca770b60e" :answer-field/id #uuid "71b478d5-40d3-56c6-919f-e4aca770b60e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4bcba26e-b5e7-51d8-9a3e-8c8e00c7d593" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1347198e-7062-5143-bac3-b619f4969e12" "answer-a0deb69e-60ce-5af0-98d7-4bcde1e624aa" "answer-4bcba26e-b5e7-51d8-9a3e-8c8e00c7d593" "answer-06efb0b9-ff81-5d60-949a-63d7901766a4" "answer-02218168-6841-5f87-b459-2ef8ded18fa1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1347198e-7062-5143-bac3-b619f4969e12" :answer/id #uuid "1347198e-7062-5143-bac3-b619f4969e12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a0deb69e-60ce-5af0-98d7-4bcde1e624aa" :answer/id #uuid "a0deb69e-60ce-5af0-98d7-4bcde1e624aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4bcba26e-b5e7-51d8-9a3e-8c8e00c7d593" :answer/id #uuid "4bcba26e-b5e7-51d8-9a3e-8c8e00c7d593" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06efb0b9-ff81-5d60-949a-63d7901766a4" :answer/id #uuid "06efb0b9-ff81-5d60-949a-63d7901766a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-02218168-6841-5f87-b459-2ef8ded18fa1" :answer/id #uuid "02218168-6841-5f87-b459-2ef8ded18fa1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8f2a8490-6351-51db-83b8-81572c8b1d30" :question/id #uuid "8f2a8490-6351-51db-83b8-81572c8b1d30" :question/math-academy-id "q-134029" :question/problem "![](images/e2/e2154f7bdd31e0c35517051fe46764ab75e597d0d78dbc64ffc55d1faecbec78.png)\n\nEstimate the equation of the trend line for the scatter plot above. Round both the slope and the $y$-intercept to the nearest $0.5.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot:\n\n![](images/68/687b257b9e2c6d3d2a015a5703d4fc29e9ab0598fb7e7ac69b588334c4a1e73d.png)\n\nIt seems that the trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})≈(2,4)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})≈(6,6).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we estimate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ≈\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6-4}{6-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{4} \\\\  & =0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=0.5$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=0.5x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to estimate the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can do this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(2,4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =0.5x+b \\\\ 4 & =0.5(2)+b \\\\ 4 & =1+b \\\\ 3 & =b \\\\ b & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=0.5x+3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-16786d6f-ad61-5cf1-a755-78c7e48129ac"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-16786d6f-ad61-5cf1-a755-78c7e48129ac" :answer-field/id #uuid "16786d6f-ad61-5cf1-a755-78c7e48129ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9737ccf3-fccb-59bd-8554-c4d39bf5417f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-965db60e-03bc-5816-9108-a20a96a20071" "answer-cc5b411d-5258-56ac-82df-1a19c550b5ae" "answer-9737ccf3-fccb-59bd-8554-c4d39bf5417f" "answer-6d7e6c7d-9523-5d3a-9512-3303d59336bb" "answer-ed9fae53-d1eb-5b69-9068-61eacfbae378"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-965db60e-03bc-5816-9108-a20a96a20071" :answer/id #uuid "965db60e-03bc-5816-9108-a20a96a20071" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-0.5x+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cc5b411d-5258-56ac-82df-1a19c550b5ae" :answer/id #uuid "cc5b411d-5258-56ac-82df-1a19c550b5ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-x+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9737ccf3-fccb-59bd-8554-c4d39bf5417f" :answer/id #uuid "9737ccf3-fccb-59bd-8554-c4d39bf5417f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=0.5x+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d7e6c7d-9523-5d3a-9512-3303d59336bb" :answer/id #uuid "6d7e6c7d-9523-5d3a-9512-3303d59336bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=0.5x-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ed9fae53-d1eb-5b69-9068-61eacfbae378" :answer/id #uuid "ed9fae53-d1eb-5b69-9068-61eacfbae378" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x+5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-07871eb6-b857-5072-89f4-ba9b4061b1b7" :question/id #uuid "07871eb6-b857-5072-89f4-ba9b4061b1b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-134028" :question/problem "![](images/2d/2ddf870155c876bac41bd437229afb971bcb6eb6cdd67351c27a0132f7d05325.png)\n\nEstimate the slope of the trend line for the scatter plot above. Round your answer to the nearest $0.5.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot:\n\n![](images/b7/b79dacf04634d91eae5ee8dd82a6603ed93357d6300a95e6343a683429caf506.png)\n\nIt seems that the trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})≈(4,6)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})≈(8,4).$\n\nTherefore, we estimate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ≈\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-6}{8-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{4} \\\\  & =-0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-db4bfec2-e156-5a49-b929-8f51580bf008"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-db4bfec2-e156-5a49-b929-8f51580bf008" :answer-field/id #uuid "db4bfec2-e156-5a49-b929-8f51580bf008" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-36fff2b4-d8f8-5391-8f3d-f1aa18360507" :answer-field/choices ["answer-36fff2b4-d8f8-5391-8f3d-f1aa18360507" "